{"id":"G1260","lemma":"διαλογίζομαι","transliteration":"dialogizomai","sayIt":"dialogizomai","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to discuss","meaning":"δια-λογίζομαι, depon.\n[in LXX chiefly for חשׁב, frequently in Pss. ;]\n1. to balance accounts (Dem.).\n2. to consider, reason (Isocr.): Luk.1:29 5:21; ἐν τ. καρδία, Mrk.2:6, 8, Luk.5:22; περί Luk.3:15; ἐν ἑαυτῷ (-οῖς), Mat.16:7-8, Mrk.2:8, Luk.12:17; πρὸς ἑ., Mrk.9:33 11:31, Luk.20:14; παρ᾽ ἑ., Mat.21:25 (ἐν ἑ., T, WH, mg.); πρὸς ἀλλήλους, Mrk.8:16; ὅτι, Mrk.8:17, Jhn.11:50, Rec. (DB, i, 611; Cremer, 400).†\n(AS)","glosses":["debating","deliberated","thinking","discussed this","began to discuss","discussing"],"count":15,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"They discussed this","kjv":"they reasoned"}},{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you debating","kjv":"reason ye"}},{"chapterId":"mat-21","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"They deliberated","kjv":"they reasoned"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-2","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"thinking","kjv":"reasoning"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-2","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"they were thinking","kjv":"reasoned"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-8","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"they began to discuss","kjv":"they reasoned"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-8","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you debating","kjv":"reason ye"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-9","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"were you discussing","kjv":"was it that ye disputed"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-11","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"They deliberated"}},{"chapterId":"luk-1","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"wondered","kjv":"cast in her mind"}},{"chapterId":"luk-3","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"wondering","kjv":"mused"}},{"chapterId":"luk-5","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"thinking to themselves","kjv":"to reason"}},{"chapterId":"luk-5","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"are you thinking these things","kjv":"reason ye"}},{"chapterId":"luk-12","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"he thought","kjv":"he thought"}},{"chapterId":"luk-20","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"they discussed it","kjv":"they reasoned"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 16:7","note":"They reasoned among themselves, saying, “We brought no bread.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Mark 2:6","note":"But there were some of the scribes sitting there, and reasoning in their hearts,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 1:29","note":"But when she saw him, she was greatly troubled at the saying, and considered what kind of salutation this might be.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}